Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.21,0:00:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.55,0:00:22.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh! Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.11,0:00:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.36,0:00:40.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh! Yu-Gi-Oh
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.51,0:01:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.49,0:01:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,prove that you're worthy of your reputation\Nand take down his Egyptian God card.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.47,0:01:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless you don't have what it takes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.99,0:01:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe your Duelist Kingdom\NChampionship victory was just a fluke.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.25,0:01:16.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I will defeat him, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.43,0:01:17.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I assure you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.97,0:01:19.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Marek, it's over. Ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.03,0:01:22.37,Default,,0,0,0,,My Egyptian God card is unstoppable.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.03,0:01:26.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And you're my next victim, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.05,0:01:31.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Once Slifer the Sky\NDragon annihilates Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.07,0:01:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm coming after your Egyptian God card!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.03,0:01:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Save your breath!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.35,0:01:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Your empty threats don't scare me!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.91,0:01:40.95,Default,,0,0,0,,They will in time, fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.83,0:01:44.19,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel isn't over yet, Merrick!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.45,0:01:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got to figure out a way to\Ndefeat his Egyptian God card!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.73,0:01:49.89,Default,,0,0,0,,But it has 10,000 attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.09,0:01:52.47,Default,,0,0,0,,None of my monsters\Neven come close to that!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.55,0:01:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, it grows stronger\Nwith every card he draws!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.01,0:01:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,but it must have some\Nweakness, and I'll find it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.55,0:01:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.79,0:02:01.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.70,0:02:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Monster Reborn could come in handy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.11,0:02:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I place one card face down,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.01,0:02:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,and I summon Big Shield\NGardener in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.07,0:02:17.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you've\Nforgotten that by summoning
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.59,0:02:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,a monster you activate my\Ndragon's special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.67,0:02:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me remind you by\Nblasting your monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.03,0:02:31.71,Default,,0,0,0,,This surge of energy from my\Ndragon's second mouth will
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.79,0:02:35.41,Default,,0,0,0,,drain your big shield Gardner\Nof 2,000 defense points.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.59,0:02:37.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Yuki won't last much longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.81,0:02:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,He better last long enough for me\Nto learn Slifer the Sky Dragon's.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.95,0:02:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,weakness so I can defeat it later\Nand add it to my collection.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.71,0:02:47.06,Default,,0,0,0,,How's he gonna do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.21,0:02:49.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That dragon's power keeps growing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.39,0:02:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, check it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.19,0:02:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yuki's monster survived\Nthe attack. Barely.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.11,0:02:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Your big shield has been cut down to size,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.31,0:03:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,and my Egyptian God card will\Ncontinue to automatically
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.91,0:03:04.73,Default,,0,0,0,,devastate your monsters as soon\Nas they're summoned to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.09,0:03:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Just one more attack and your\Nonly defense will be demolished,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.95,0:03:12.21,Default,,0,0,0,,leaving nothing in between you and Slifer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.29,0:03:14.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's your faith in\Nthe cards now, Pharaoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.13,0:03:18.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Now observe while I draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.71,0:03:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And as you know, Slifer gets 1,000\Nattack points for every card in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.11,0:03:29.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I count 11, giving my\Ndragon 11,000 attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.51,0:03:34.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, 11,000 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.19,0:03:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That's already more than three times the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.25,0:03:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,attack strength of your\Nblue-eyes white dragon,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.71,0:03:40.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Seto.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.62,0:03:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And it'll only get stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.35,0:03:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's opponent has\Ninfinite cards in play,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.87,0:03:47.64,Default,,0,0,0,,allowing him to hold as\Nmany cards as he wants.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.11,0:03:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And the more cards in his hand, the\Nmore attack points his dragon has.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.89,0:03:56.41,Default,,0,0,0,,That means there's no limit to how\Nstrong his Egyptian God card can grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.83,0:03:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Or is there? Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.19,0:04:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Slifer's power depends on how many\Ncards the player has in his entire deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.31,0:04:05.15,Default,,0,0,0,,That's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.79,0:04:09.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Slifer the Sky Dragon has one fatal flaw.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.19,0:04:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's see if Yugi is\Nduelist enough to figure it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.49,0:04:16.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now my Sky Dragon, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.79,0:04:18.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Eradicate his shield!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.41,0:04:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The only thing that stands in\Nthe way of his destruction!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.89,0:04:25.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon that puzzle, and\Nthe world, will be mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.35,0:04:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I know exactly how to defeat\Nthis Egyptian God card,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.69,0:04:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,but let's see if you be smart\Nenough to figure it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.29,0:04:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You're completely defenseless, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.77,0:04:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The next time my Sky Dragon\Nattacks, you'll be finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.05,0:04:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,It's undefeatable, you fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.09,0:04:44.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't let Merrick win my puzzle, but\NI've never faced anything so powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.51,0:04:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And the more cards he\Ndraws, the stronger it gets.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.71,0:04:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, and that's how I'll defeat it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.75,0:04:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I will make Slifer destroy itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.19,0:04:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,About time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.71,0:04:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.95,0:04:57.66,Default,,0,0,0,,What makes you think you can?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.61,0:05:00.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a simple matter of common sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.15,0:05:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,If all of my monsters are too weak, then\NI must use your monster to destroy itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.01,0:05:11.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Haven't you realized yet that an\NEgyptian god card cannot be controlled?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.15,0:05:13.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's much too powerful, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.07,0:05:15.07,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.35,0:05:17.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps you don't have\Nas much knowledge about
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.41,0:05:19.94,Default,,0,0,0,,the Egyptian god cards\Nas you think you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.67,0:05:23.79,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you challenge my\Nwisdom of the ancient ways?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.97,0:05:24.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I know all!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.13,0:05:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll find out how much you\Nknow soon enough, Merrick.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.25,0:05:31.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to see you try\Nto turn Slifer against me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.03,0:05:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,What's Yugi talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.75,0:05:35.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, sure, he's a great duelist,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.49,0:05:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,but how can he make that\NEgyptian god card destroy itself?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.41,0:05:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,That dragon seems way\Ntoo strong to control.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.95,0:05:42.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds crazy to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.23,0:05:43.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.29,0:05:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,It's quite simple, Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.03,0:05:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The dragon's greatest strength\Nis also its greatest weakness.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.59,0:05:51.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Seto, I still don't get what's going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.91,0:05:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Time for you to make your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.07,0:05:59.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I promise it will be your last.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.35,0:06:02.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.85,0:06:04.11,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see, Merrick.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.31,0:06:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,If I don't draw the right card\Nnow, this Sky Dragon will crush me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.11,0:06:10.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I know the heart of the\Ncards will guide me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.25,0:06:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Now! Perfect!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.63,0:06:21.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.39,0:06:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Just what I need to take you down!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.51,0:06:26.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like Yugi got his card.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.19,0:06:29.15,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's only half the battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.37,0:06:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,This strategy requires perfect timing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.99,0:06:33.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not over yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.39,0:06:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to lose!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.85,0:06:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I reveal my face down card!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.27,0:06:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Monster Reborn!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.01,0:06:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What good will that do?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.71,0:06:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,This magic card allows me to bring\Nback one monster from the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.37,0:06:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose to resurrect my\Nmighty Buster Blader, return!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.03,0:06:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.01,0:07:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,My dragon's already\Ndestroyed that monster once.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.07,0:07:06.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, summoning it to defend your life\Npoints will only delay your ultimate defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.71,0:07:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not defending.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.39,0:07:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a closer look, Marek.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.79,0:07:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Buster Blader has been\Nsummoned in attack mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.93,0:07:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,what a thoughtless move\Nwith his buster blader in
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.25,0:07:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,attack mode my dragon's blast\Nwill not only annihilate
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.21,0:07:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,his monster it'll wipe\Nout the rest of his life
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.83,0:07:29.59,Default,,0,0,0,,points winning his millennium\Npuzzle was a simpler
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.67,0:07:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,task than i thought i\Nknow i can't win by just
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.95,0:07:36.21,Default,,0,0,0,,defending my points that's\Nwhy i'm risking this entire
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.29,0:07:40.21,Default,,0,0,0,,duel on one final sword\Nattack by buster blader you're
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.29,0:07:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,More of a fool than I\Nthought. You've left yourself
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.95,0:07:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,wide open for my egyptian\Ngod card to defeat you
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.15,0:07:50.45,Default,,0,0,0,,have you forgotten about my\Nfive card combination that
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.53,0:07:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,makes life for the sky dragon\Ncompletely indestructible
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.69,0:07:57.35,Default,,0,0,0,,perhaps you need a\Nreminder pharaoh first my
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.43,0:08:00.65,Default,,0,0,0,,card of safe return allows\Nme to draw three cards
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.73,0:08:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,whenever a monster is\Nrevived since you resurrected
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.39,0:08:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,buster later i can now draw\Nthree I need more cards
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.19,0:08:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,from my deck to increase the\Nnumber of cards in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.15,0:08:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, and the more cards you hold, the\Nstronger your dragon becomes. Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.45,0:08:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,So Slifer gains 3,000\Nadditional attack points,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.43,0:08:23.25,Default,,0,0,0,,giving it a total of 14,000 attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.83,0:08:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,14,000 attack points?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.05,0:08:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's nuts! And then,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.49,0:08:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,you forgot that bringing\NBuster Blader back from
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.05,0:08:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,the graveyard activates\NSlyper's second mouth!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.65,0:08:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Blasting 2,000 attack points\Naway from your monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.19,0:08:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Buster Blader's strong enough\Nto survive your attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.63,0:08:49.61,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the beginning of\Nthe end for you, Pharaoh!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.95,0:08:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,My Egyptian God card has\Nweakened your monster
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.71,0:08:55.77,Default,,0,0,0,,into the pathetic mess\Nbarely standing before you!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.79,0:08:59.53,Default,,0,0,0,,My next attack will\Nfinish you off forever!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.03,0:09:04.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Buster Blader may\Nhave survived that blast,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.09,0:09:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,but it's still no match\Nfor my Egyptian God card.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.15,0:09:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your reign as pharaoh is almost over,\Nso prepare to surrender your puzzle.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.95,0:09:16.85,Default,,0,0,0,,In my next turn, your monster and your\Nlife points will be completely wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.07,0:09:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid that there isn't\Ngoing to be a next turn for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.69,0:09:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Once Buster Flader attacks your Egyptian\NGod card, you'll be defeated, Merrick.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.55,0:09:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now watch as my plan to slay your\Nso-called indestructible dragon begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.07,0:09:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Has Yugi lost it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.91,0:09:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,His Buster Blader won't even\Nscratch Slifer the Sky Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.07,0:09:42.97,Default,,0,0,0,,If Yu-Gi's plan works, my suspicions about\Nhow to defeat Slifer will be confirmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.37,0:09:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Time for me to win this duel right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.15,0:09:49.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm ready for your pathetic\Nattack. This is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.47,0:09:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone's about to lose this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.85,0:09:56.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Buster Blader, attack Slifer the\NSky Dragon with your powerful blade!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.53,0:10:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Watching your puny warrior trying to\Ntake down my unstoppable Egyptian.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.87,0:10:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,god card is actually quite amusing\Nhave you forgotten that my sky
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.57,0:10:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,dragon is protected by my ultimate\Ndefender the shape shifting revival gem
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.95,0:10:21.95,Default,,0,0,0,,your
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.45,0:10:23.28,Default,,0,0,0,,attack's
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.36,0:10:24.19,Default,,0,0,0,,been blocked and
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.27,0:10:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,my revival gem will reform itself now
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.99,0:10:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,After that,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.07,0:10:33.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I can draw yet another three cards and\NSlyper's power will grow even greater!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.87,0:10:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Preparing itself to destroy\Nyou once and for all with
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.91,0:10:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,a force more intense than\Nanything you've ever seen!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.99,0:10:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid that it's still my turn,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.93,0:10:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,but before I make my next move,\NI need Revival Gem to revive!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.35,0:10:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Observe!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.61,0:10:51.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And now the stage is set for this card!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.53,0:10:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,The magic card, Brain Control.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.17,0:10:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll control your monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.41,0:11:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I get Yugi's plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.97,0:11:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He must want to use Brain Control\Nto take over the dragon's mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.17,0:11:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,but I still think Slyfer's way\Ntoo strong to be controlled.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.57,0:11:14.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not quite that simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.73,0:11:15.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, Yami.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.33,0:11:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid all magic cards are\Ncompletely ineffective against Egyptian
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.55,0:11:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,God monsters, and now you'll pay the\Nprice for making such a foolish mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.35,0:11:37.95,Default,,0,0,0,,don't be so sure who told you I\Nwas after your dragon you're not no
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.03,0:11:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Merrick, there's another monster on your\Nfield I'm after, and I'll control him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.69,0:11:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,My Brain Control card will\Nseize your Revival Jam!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.23,0:11:53.59,Default,,0,0,0,,What can you possibly do\Nwith my Revival Jam card?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.11,0:11:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It can't hurt my dragon,\Nso it's of no use to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.95,0:11:59.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You still don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.59,0:12:03.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Since Revival Jam reformed, draw\Nyour three new cards, Merrick.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.35,0:12:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I will, which raises my Egyptian God\Ncard another 3,000 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.37,0:12:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,With every card I draw, my\Nmonster will get even stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.69,0:12:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,One, two, three.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.83,0:12:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That brings Slyfer's\Nattack points to 17,000.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.93,0:12:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, Barrow, the time for me\Nto destroy you has finally arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.05,0:12:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Slifer, wipe out his Buster\NBlader and his life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.95,0:12:31.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Merrick.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.65,0:12:35.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Sky Dragon's special ability\Nmeans its second mouth has
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.39,0:12:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,to attack any new monster that\Nappears on my side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.85,0:12:46.99,Default,,0,0,0,,That means before you can destroy me,\Nyour monster must attack my Revival Jam.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.81,0:12:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what happens now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.15,0:12:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Revival Jam revives itself again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.41,0:13:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And each time a monster regenerates,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.95,0:13:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,you have to draw three more\Ncards from your dueling deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.45,0:13:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.03,0:13:17.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever Revival Jam reappears on the\Nfield, my dragon automatically attacks it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.13,0:13:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And since Yami controls Revival Jam,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.51,0:13:25.45,Default,,0,0,0,,it will revive itself on his side of the\Nfield, which makes me draw three new cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.55,0:13:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Then my dragon will attack again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.95,0:13:31.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Each event triggers the next\Nin a never-ending cycle.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.01,0:13:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,First, attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.21,0:13:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, regenerate.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.65,0:13:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,then draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.97,0:13:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,My Egyptian god card will continue to grow
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.79,0:13:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,stronger with each cycle\Nas I draw more cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.09,0:13:49.56,Default,,0,0,0,,But it doesn't matter because I'm trapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.25,0:13:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.95,0:13:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, Merrick.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.01,0:13:57.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Once you run out of cards to draw,\Nyou will automatically lose this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.87,0:13:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.89,0:14:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be happening.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.83,0:14:05.49,Default,,0,0,0,,As powerful as your Egyptian god card is,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.57,0:14:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,no monster is without weakness\Nand the sky dragon's flaw
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.51,0:14:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Lies within its special ability,\Nits second mouth attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.09,0:14:20.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no control over\Nmy Egyptian god monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.83,0:14:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,as long as yami's rave\Ncontrol is in effect
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.61,0:14:26.55,Default,,0,0,0,,my dragon will keep\Nattacking revival jam and
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.63,0:14:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,my mind slave will keep\Ndrawing cards until
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.85,0:14:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.57,0:14:34.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I turned your dragon against you,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.29,0:14:38.51,Default,,0,0,0,,causing you to use up all the\Ncards in your dueling deck. No!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.03,0:14:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That means I win. It's over!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.89,0:14:48.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.79,0:14:52.29,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I lose with an\NEgyptian god card in my deck?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.63,0:14:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll pay, Yami.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.63,0:14:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,You may have defeated Sleightheart,\Nbut I hold another Egyptian god card,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.05,0:15:02.15,Default,,0,0,0,,a much more powerful one.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.51,0:15:09.65,Default,,0,0,0,,So savor this victory while you\Ncan, for it will be your last.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.93,0:15:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi won the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.55,0:15:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What a totally awesome comeback.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.73,0:15:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Hand over your Egyptian god card to Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.37,0:15:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Tournament rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.55,0:15:23.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, snap out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.93,0:15:27.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, no one likes to lose,\Nbut rules are rules, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.05,0:15:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, don't be so hard on yourself, mister.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.33,0:15:31.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.55,0:15:33.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, there it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.71,0:15:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,His life of the Sky Dragon's awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.55,0:15:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish Seto and I could keep it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.49,0:15:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But as commissioner of the\NBattle City Tournament,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.17,0:15:46.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to hand this card over\Nto you, Yugi, and you earned it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.29,0:15:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's not all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.69,0:15:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You get his locator card also.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.77,0:15:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Just don't get too attached, because my\Nbrother's got his eye on that dragon, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.29,0:16:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,So watch out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.35,0:16:02.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I must be careful with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.31,0:16:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, so you figured out how to\Ndefeat Slifer the Sky Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.83,0:16:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.05,0:16:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a real shame you\Nwon't have it for too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.25,0:16:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.45,0:16:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Because you and I are going\Nto duel for it right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.47,0:16:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, when I defeat you, Slifer the\NSky Dragon will be where it belongs.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.21,0:16:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,In my deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.11,0:16:25.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You see,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.02,0:16:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm already in possession of one Egyptian\Ngod card and I plan to win the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.09,0:16:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's time to duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.25,0:16:36.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Once I win Slifer from you,\NI'll only need one more.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.65,0:16:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll be the number\None duelist in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.01,0:16:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Silly fools!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.85,0:16:46.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.76,0:16:49.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I've had enough of your\Nmind tricks, Merrick!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.19,0:16:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time for you to show yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.63,0:16:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Not to worry, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.49,0:16:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll meet me sooner than you think.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.85,0:16:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm on my way to Battle City as we speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.43,0:17:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Once I'm there, the next\Nphase of my plan begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.49,0:17:06.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I assure you the power of\Nthe Pharaoh will be mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.55,0:17:11.13,Default,,0,0,0,,My loyal mind servants are\Npreparing for my arrival right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.49,0:17:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are they, Merrick?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.07,0:17:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I have rare hunters\Neverywhere in Battle City.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.05,0:17:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And I can see all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.07,0:17:22.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I see the Millennium\NPuzzle that will be mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.69,0:17:25.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I see a defenseless city\Nwaiting to be conquered.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.05,0:17:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And I see potential mine\Nslaves in every crowd.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.63,0:17:34.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm always searching for new servants\Nto add to my army of rare hunters.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.53,0:17:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder who'll be next.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.41,0:17:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Aw, man, I was this close to\Nkicking Kaiba's butt in a duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.71,0:17:44.53,Default,,0,0,0,,So why did you look so relieved when\Nhe had to suddenly take off? What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.69,0:17:47.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not afraid of that punk. Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.83,0:17:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,So tell me, Farrow, which of your friends\Nwould make the best mind slave? Teya?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.79,0:17:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.21,0:17:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You leave them alone. Understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.49,0:17:58.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm warning you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.01,0:18:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it appears I've hit your\Nsensitive spot, haven't I, Farrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.83,0:18:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps I can use your friends to get\Nwhat I want from you, namely your puzzle.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.43,0:18:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And the Egyptian God Card\Nyou've won, I told you,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.69,0:18:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,leave my friends out of\Nthis Or else you'll what?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.99,0:18:18.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Your friends are\Nmeaningless to me Besides,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.79,0:18:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I have nothing to lose And\Nthe whole world to gain
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.27,0:18:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not test me If any harm befalls\Nmy friends, you will regret it,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.25,0:18:32.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Merrick They did nothing to you,\Nso you settle your score with me
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.47,0:18:37.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Just as my dragon's one\Nweakness destroyed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.59,0:18:40.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Your loyalty to our friends\Nwill soon destroy you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.63,0:18:43.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Marek, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.91,0:18:45.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I must save them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.59,0:18:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, get back here right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.09,0:18:53.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Our duel will have to wait, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.01,0:18:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,My friends are in great danger,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.47,0:19:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,and their safety is more important\Nto me than anything in this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.19,0:19:03.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.31,0:19:06.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Running away from a challenge\Nis against tournament rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.93,0:19:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally I have arrived. I may have\Nlost one of my two Egyptian god
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.89,0:19:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,cards to yavi but no matter with\Nthe power of the millennium rod
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.91,0:19:25.19,Default,,0,0,0,,in my hand and his precious\Nfriends at my disposal i'll get
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.27,0:19:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,everything i desire i gotta find my
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.45,0:19:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,friends before merrick gets to them
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.77,0:19:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,this time the pharaoh's\Nin a battle he can't
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.45,0:19:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,win soon the egyptian\Ngod card he took from me
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.69,0:19:49.13,Default,,0,0,0,,and his millennium puzzle\Nwill be mine then i'll
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.21,0:19:52.45,Default,,0,0,0,,be pharaoh and the world\Nwill cower at my feet
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.63,0:20:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
